      section: "CS",
      q: "A processor has 64 general-purpose registers and 50 distinct instruction types. An instruction is encoded in 32-bits. What is the maximum number of bits that can be used to store the immediate operand for the given instruction? ADD R1, #25 // R1 = R1 + 25",
      options: ["16","20","22","24"],
